<meta>
<title | Bibliography and external DSLs>
<author | Test Author>
<abstract |
This fixture exercises slice 5d: structured bibliography emission as
JATS `<element-citation>` (per-field author/title/source/volume/etc.)
plus external-DSL JATS treatment (mermaid/abc as `<fig>` with
`<preformat>` source preservation).
>
</meta>

<data>
<library |
@article{Smith2020,
  author = {Smith, Jane and Doe, John},
  title  = {On the Behavior of Elephants},
  journal = {Journal of Pachyderm Studies},
  year   = 2020,
  volume = 12,
  number = 3,
  pages  = {45--67},
  doi    = {10.1234/jps.2020.45}
}
@book{Jones2018,
  author = {Jones, Alice},
  title  = {Methods in Field Research},
  publisher = {Academic Press},
  year   = 2018,
  address = {New York}
}
@inproceedings{Brown2021,
  author = {Brown, Bob and Green, Carol},
  title  = {New Algorithms for Diagram Layout},
  booktitle = {Proceedings of the 2021 Symposium on Layout},
  year   = 2021,
  pages  = {100--110}
}
>
</data>

<section | Introduction>

This section cites Smith and Doe <cite @Smith2020> and the Jones
field-research textbook <cite @Jones2018>. A third citation points
to the diagram-layout paper <cite @Brown2021>.

<section | Diagrams>

A Mermaid flowchart with a caption (cross-referenced as <ref @fig:flow>):

<mermaid #fig:flow caption="A simple Mermaid flowchart.">
graph TD;
  A[Start] --> B{Decision};
  B -->|yes| C[Do thing];
  B -->|no|  D[Skip];
</mermaid>

